{
  "name": "Transcribe audio and video to Google Drive notes with Apify Whisper and GPT",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "85e2c39b-4dfa-4e0c-8c97-2bf40d03c292",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -624,
        -176
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 496,
        "height": 928,
        "content": "## Audio and video to searchable Markdown notes\n\n### How it works\n\n1. You open the built-in n8n form and paste one or more media links: podcast episodes, webinar recordings, MP3 or MP4 files, or any of the hundreds of sources yt-dlp understands.\n2. The [Universal Media Transcriber](https://apify.com/sauliusautomatesit/media-transcriber) Actor on Apify runs Whisper over every file (90+ languages, no OpenAI key needed for the transcription itself) and returns text plus timestamped segments.\n3. Because the Actor is started asynchronously and polled, files of any length are safe - a three-hour recording will not time out.\n4. An LLM turns each transcript into a summary, key points, action items and topic tags.\n5. Each file becomes a Markdown note in Google Drive and a row in a Google Sheet index, so old recordings stay findable. Files that could not be transcribed are logged with their error rather than dropped.\n\n### Setup\n\n- [ ] Create a free Apify account and copy your API token from Settings, API & Integrations.\n- [ ] Add an **HTTP Header Auth** credential: name `Authorization`, value `Bearer YOUR_APIFY_TOKEN`. Select it on all three Apify HTTP nodes.\n- [ ] Connect your OpenAI, Google Drive and Google Sheets credentials.\n- [ ] Create a Google Sheet with the header row listed on the sticky note above the logging nodes and paste its id into **Settings**.\n\n### Customization\n\nSwap the OpenAI chat model node for Gemini, Anthropic or Ollama. Change the Whisper size in the form (`tiny` to `medium`) to trade speed for accuracy. Replace Google Drive with Notion, Slack or S3 if that is where your notes live."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "2707c3b9-1447-4666-8262-1e7835b18888",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -48,
        -128
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 624,
        "height": 288,
        "content": "## Collect the request\n\nThe form takes the media links, the Whisper model size and an optional language. The Settings node holds everything else you need to configure."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ed338a40-f302-4631-8882-cd77ffaade22",
      "name": "Sticky Note2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        576,
        -128
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 880,
        "height": 688,
        "content": "## Transcribe on Apify, however long it takes\n\nThe Actor is started asynchronously and polled until it finishes, so long recordings never hit the five-minute limit of the synchronous endpoint. A failed or stuck run stops the workflow with a readable error."
